  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Puerto Rican politically committed song movement of the late 1960s and 1970s, tied to the independence movement and university circles in San Juan. Singers such as Roy Brown and Andrés Jiménez and the group Haciendo Punto en Otro Son set topical texts to guitar and the cuatro, drawing on jíbaro forms such as the seis and aguinaldo, and early albums of the movement appeared on the independent Disco Libre label.",
